[4] Fixed-margin / Johnson-sector protocol from arXiv:2606.22636
  Imported proof pattern:
    binary relation with fixed margins
      -> local 2x2 swaps / two-row heat-bath comparison
      -> reduction to three rows
      -> scalar count sector + Johnson harmonic sectors
  LRC14 translation:
    binary relation = speeds versus packet lenses
      lenses: q clocks, boundary owners, C27 shells, unital pairs,
              K33 owners, exact-period packets, boundary-moment signs
    fixed margins = reductions that preserve source-spectrum labels
    scalar sector = qdiv, exact M/Farey node, Haar mass
    Johnson sectors = non-scalar owner/carry/state-lift labels
  Proof obligation:
    show every fixed-margin packet component reaches F0-F5 by swaps,
    unless a three-row Johnson sector is a genuine F7 falsifier.

