[6] Readout
  Labelled Packet Theorem target:
    Every primitive LRC14 row is in F0-F5, or is an F6 non-migrating
    boundary-moment kernel, unless a new F7 Johnson sector exists.
  Therefore an actual counterexample must be:
    qdiv>=14, no strict Haar-open witness, not AP/GW boundary-only,
    not unit-petal, not positive K33, and zero/nonpositive under the
    boundary-moment bridge.
  The current gauntlets find no such packet in the audited AP atlas.
